/*
  KG-QL: Q-Learning Illuminance Controller Agent

  JaCaMo project file for the Gradle task "taskQl".

  Starts one BDI agent, illuminance_controller_agent_ql
  (src/agt/illuminance_controller_agent_ql.asl), which trains a tabular
  Q-learning policy for the lamps and blinds of the lab selected by the active
  profile (profiles are defined in src/agt/lab_profiles.asl). The Q-table and
  the training logs are written to files at the end of training; the benchmark
  agent (task_bench.jcm) later evaluates the stored Q-table.

  To run: ./gradlew taskQl -Pprofile=<profile id>
          (while the Node-RED simulator flow of that profile is running; the
          port of each lab is the sim_port in lab_profiles.asl, for example
          1881 for the custom lab)

  Options:
    -Pprofile=<id>   Lab profile; passed as the system property active.profile.
                     Without it the active_profile belief of the agent is used.
    use_stereotypes  Knowledge-guided (true) or plain (false) Q-learning is
                     chosen by the belief use_stereotypes(true/false) in
                     illuminance_controller_agent_ql.asl. For a single manual
                     run edit that belief; the full-run script
                     run_full_project.ps1 rewrites it for each arm.
*/

mas lab_ql {

    agent illuminance_controller_agent_ql

}
